  "name": "two-pair-equal-reboot-a-secondary",
  "lab": "Medium lab",
  "title": "Pair A secondary reboot \u00b7 two MLAG pairs, equal bridge priority 0x8000",
  "action": "Resets the data bridge on all four CHRs over management SSH with protocol-mode=rstp and bridge priority 0x8000 on all four CHRs, as in the field report where every MLAG pair kept the same priority. Pair A (CHR 1 MLAG primary, CHR 2 MLAG secondary) and pair B (CHR 3 MLAG primary, CHR 4 MLAG secondary) are joined by one distributed LACP bond, mlag-id 11 on pair A and 21 on pair B. Host 1 bonds to pair B and host 2 to pair A, so both VLAN 110 streams cross both pairs. It requires a loss-free baseline with root 0x8000.02:00:00:21:00:11 on all four CHRs. It then reboots CHR 2 (pair A's MLAG secondary) with `/system reboot`, waits for the guest uptime to reset and keeps probing for 16 s plus a 3 s recovery window.",
